    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S714\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\nactions of the Port Washington union free school district with respect\nto certain building aid contracts\n\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\nTo remedy a ministerial filing error on the part of the port\nWashington Union Free School District in relation to their eligibility\nfor state aid.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 provides for the legislative intent on the legislation.\n\nSection 2 legalizes, validates, ratifies and confirms the Port\nWashington Union Free School District's compliance with the\nrequirements set forth so that they shall receive the appropriate\nstate aid previously allotted to them.\n\nSection 3 provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Port Washington Union Free School District approved several\ncapital improvement projects through the State Education Department\nwhich were deemed eligible for state aid. Due to ministerial error,\nhowever, the proper filing for such aid was never accomplished, and\nthus, the District became ineligible for such aid. This legislation\nseeks to rectify that situation.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-08: Referred to Rules\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
